Wait: 2.3.2's getZipLib checks `typeof fflate === "object" && fflate` (script-scoped global var: in the browser userscript, `fflate` comes from @require as a global). In jsdom `window.eval` — `typeof fflate` would look up window.fflate (global scope), yes fine. Then `zipSync(entries,{level:6})` returns Uint8Array. Real fflate's will produce real zip. 

So: in the harness, set `window.fflate = { strToU8: fflate.strToU8, zipSync: fflate.zipSync }` — but careful: for 2.4.0, `typeof window.fflate` is now set too; but 2.4's getZipLib prefers EMBEDDED_FFLATE, so no behavior change. Keep.

